  "reasoning_log_text": "The study presents a computational model (DPC) demonstrating hierarchical temporal representations. Evidence for prediction error minimization and hierarchical abstraction is strong across both LO/GO contexts (e.g., Fig 2, Fig 3). Key findings include V1-like receptive fields (Fig 2c), hierarchical timescale separation ($\tau_{rh} > \tau_r$ in Fig 3a, 0.6), and the ability to model prediction/postdiction (Fig 4). The three-level model further demonstrates learning higher-order dynamics (bouncing type) (Fig 6g, 0.8). Evidence for feedforward propagation is implied by the error flow (Fig 1e, 0.6). Ubiquity factors are addressed through hierarchical structure demonstrations across levels (Fig 3, Fig 6)."
